            "use_h1": false
          }
        },
        "en_test_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A mannequin fitted with temperature sensors is dressed in a long-sleeve base layer and full-length long underwear, placed inside the sleeping bag, and laid on a camping pad.</p><p>Sensors at five points on the mannequin measure how much heat it loses. Those readings and the lab's air temperature go into a formula that calculates the ratings.</p><p>A sleeping bag's warmth depends on more than the amount of fill. Fabric type and thickness, zippers, and other details all play a part, so the test evaluates the bag as a whole.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
